{"slug":"chop-shop","title":"Chop Shop","blurb":"sampling-style primitives on 1890s marches: a drum loop sliced into eighths and re-sequenced, a drum kit assembled from one-shots in two recordings, sliced horns following the chords, all swung like a sampler at 58%.","score":"examples/chop-shop.apr","code":"# Chop Shop \u2014 sampling-style primitives on 1890s marches: a drum loop sliced into eighths and\n# re-sequenced, a drum kit assembled from one-shots in two recordings, sliced horns following the\n# chords, all swung like a sampler at 58%.\ntempo 88\nkey F mixolydian\nsamples ../samples\n\nclip brk    = marine-band/stems/Thunderer/drums.wav  loop-1  warp beats\nclip horns  = marine-band/stems/Thunderer/other.wav  loop-2\nclip tdrums = marine-band/stems/Thunderer/drums.wav\nclip pdrums = marine-band/stems/WashingtonPost/drums.wav\nclip band   = marine-band/Thunderer.mp3\n\nkit b = slice brk by beats 0.5         # eighth-note slices of the drum loop\nkit h = slice horns by beats 1         # one slice per beat of the horn loop\n\nkit drums\n  kick  = tdrums  beats 62..62.5      # the loudest beats in each drum stem\n  snare = pdrums  beats 70..70.5\n  crash = band  shot-3\n\nchords I7 . IV7 . | I7 . V7 IV7\n\ntrack b            steps \"1 _ 2 _ 3 _ 3 4 | 5 _ 6 _ 7 8 7 _\"          swing 58  transpose 0\ntrack drums        steps \"kick . . . snare . . kick | . kick . . snare . . .\"  swing 58  transpose 0  volume -3\ntrack h            steps \"1 . . 3 . . 2 . | . . 4 . 3 . . .\"          swing 58  follow  filter hp 250  bars 5-8\ntrack drums.crash  at 1 5  transpose 0  volume -8\n","provenance":[{"source":"b","title":"The Thunderer \u2014 drums","kind":"loop","tracks":["b"],"recordings":[{"title":"The Thunderer","part":"drums","composed":1889,"recorded":"2017","performer":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band","credit":"\"The President's Own\" United States Marine Band, The Complete Marches of John Philip Sousa, Vol. 3.","rights":"Public domain (composit